## Frontend state (key pieces)

| State | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `form` | Paper metadata: class, subject, schoolName, examTitleId, **paperName** (version label), examType (`objective`\|`subjective`), session, duration, header/footer notes, showSectionNames, subQuestionNumberingStyle, wrapQuestionMarksInParentheses |
| `selectedQuestions` | `{ questionId, questionOrder, section, marks }` — persisted payload |
| `sectionConfigs` | `{ sectionKey, sectionName, headingText, instructionText, marksDisplayText, optionalQuestionsEnabled, optionalQuestionsAttemptCount }` — auto-created per section; `marksDisplayText` auto from `inferSectionMarksDisplay` (SAQ/LAQ optional mode uses attempt count) |
| `questionPool` | Catalog rows from API (search results only) |
| `selectedPaper` | Last saved/loaded `ExamPaperDto` snapshot |
| `generatedPapers` | List from `GET papers` (summary rows, no question bodies) |
| `suppressPaperPreload` | Blocks slot auto-load during “New Exam” setup |
| `preloadKeyRef` | Dedupes preload: `classId\|subjectId\|examTitleId\|examType\|paperName` |

**Paper slot key** (FE and BE must stay aligned):

```text
(classId, subjectId, examTitleId, normalizeExamType, normalizePaperName) → at most one paper
```

`normalizeExamTypeOption`: anything except `"subjective"` → `"objective"`.

---

## Sections model

- Section keys: `Q1`, `Q2`, … regex `^Q(\d+)$` (`SECTION_KEY_REGEX`).
- `sectionOptions` builds procedural `Q1..Qn` plus keys from configs/selection.
- Preview groups questions by `section`, sorts by `order` within section.
- Section metadata stored in `QuestionPaper.SectionMetaJson` as JSON array of `ExamSectionConfigDto`.
- Empty section on save: BE defaults to `"Q1"` for selection rows.
- **Optional questions (SAQ/LAQ only):** per-section `optionalQuestionsEnabled` + `optionalQuestionsAttemptCount` in section JSON (no new DB column). When enabled, extra instruction prints e.g. “Attempt any 5 questions.” and marks summary uses attempt count (`5x6=30` for 6 questions in pool). Paper `TotalMarks` on save counts optional sections by attempt count, not all listed questions.

