## Backend rules (`AcademicExamMakerService`)

- **Question pool**: Filters `QuestionsCatalog` by class/subject (+ optional chapters, type, category, LIKE search on stem/MCQ options). `take` clamped 20–250.
- **Create from selection**: Validates class/subject/title/**paperName**, no duplicate question IDs, unique `questionOrder > 0`, questions belong to class/subject. **Slot collision**: if paper exists for same `(classId, subjectId, examTitleId, examType, paperName)` → **400** (no silent upsert).
- **Update**: Replaces all `QuestionPaperQuestions` (remove range + new rows). Cannot change class/subject on existing id. Renaming or changing type blocked if another paper already uses that name in the same slot.
- **Generate** (`POST generate`): Blueprint random pick — **not used by compact UI**; keep for API/tests or future features.
- **Paper name**: User-supplied version label (required on create-from-selection). Optional on legacy `POST generate` (falls back to `{SubjectName} - {ExamTitle} ({dd MMM yyyy})`). DB unique index: `docs/academics_exam_maker_paper_name_unique.sql`.
- **SubQuestionNumberingStyle**: BE normalizes `numeric`/`number`/`decimal`, `alpha`/`letter`/`letters`, default `roman`.

Errors: `InvalidOperationException` → 400 with message; `DbUpdateException` → 500 with generic message (details in server logs).

---

## Math / LaTeX

`MathText` component: heuristic `looksLikeLatex` → `katex.renderToString` with `throwOnError: false`. Backslash normalization: `\\\\` → `\`. Print CSS forces KaTeX wrap (`white-space: normal`, `max-width: 100%`).

---

## Print pipeline

1. `onPrint` adds `document.body.classList.add('printing-exam-paper')`.
2. `window.print()`; removes class after 200ms.
3. `#exam-paper-print` duplicate of paper (no section editors); CSS hides everything except print host.

Section editor blocks use class `print-hidden`. Global `@page { size: A4; margin: 10mm 12mm }`.

